GPU SMMU faults: say which unit faulted and whose submission ran, and (boot-arg) let the GPU go on instead of resetting it.
Each fault now also logs FSYNR1 and UCHE_CLIENT_PF decoded like Linux a6xx_fault_handler (CP, CCU, CDP prefetch, GMU,
or the UCHE client: VFD/SP/VSC/VPC/HLSQ/PC/LRZ, TP), the CP's IB1/IB2 positions, RBBM_STATUS, CP_SCRATCH 4-7, and the
process that submitted the oldest unfinished submission (proc_selfname at submit time, 64-entry ring).
sweetgpufaultreset=0: the context bank answers faulting accesses with zeros (SCTLR without CFRE) and the fault is logged
and cleared without a reset, as under Linux msm; FAULTS does not move, so no client loses its device. A CP that does wedge
is still found by the fence wait (hang, then the usual reset). Default (unset or 1): unchanged, every fault resets the GPU.
The pm line counts the continued faults. Logged in full for the first 16 continued faults, then every 64th.

